WEBVTT

00:02:58.246 --> 00:03:01.538
Looking closer at the folds, 
we can see why.

00:03:02.288 --> 00:03:06.496
If we add a crease and number 
the new angles at this vertex,

00:03:06.496 --> 00:03:11.538
the even and odd angles no longer
add up to 180 degrees,

00:03:11.538 --> 00:03:14.038
and the model doesn’t fold flat.

00:03:14.038 --> 00:03:17.829
Finally,
a layer cannot penetrate a fold.

00:03:18.663 --> 00:03:23.204
A 2D, flat-foldable base is often
an abstract representation

00:03:23.204 --> 00:03:25.371
of a final 3D shape.

00:03:25.829 --> 00:03:30.579
Understanding the relationship
between crease patterns, 2D bases,